 "comment": "book_keeping_quality payment-channel section: two same-day invoices of one amount contend for one in-window receipt (the lower GUID takes it); an older invoice with a higher GUID takes a receipt before a newer one (date first); among two receipts the earlier-dated is tried first even with the higher GUID; receipt lags 0 and 3 match, 4 and -1 do not; next-day matches; a Sales voucher crediting the channel ledger is neither an invoice nor a receipt; an invoice's credit line on the channel ledger does not reduce its amount; a Sales voucher with a channel line and a cash line is a channel sale (its inventory line is priced in the channel bucket); months with one and four invoices; purchase rates as a year average over lines with a positive quantity and an amount (a zero, absent and negative quantity and an absent amount skipped); a sale line at exactly cost is not below it, one a float epsilon under cost is (0.3 units at 1234 paise cost 1234.0000000000002); a half-paisa rate makes the named-customer cost 12.5, rounded half to even to 12 (margin 769 bp, where half-up would give 0); sale lines with no purchase rate, a missing, zero or negative quantity, or no amount are skipped; cash-sale and named-customer buckets; the named-customer comparison margin.",
